#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Shared GitHub GET snapshot for the fleet.

One saved response serves every reader for a few minutes. The next refresh
sends If-None-Match. A 304 keeps the saved body. A rate-limit response waits
until the reset epoch from the response headers, then tries once more.

Reads of hypertask-ai/hypertask use the installation token file when it
exists. This module never prints that token.

GitHub calls per chat per hour, counted where a call reaches GitHub: a cache hit is free.

| Session id | Warn | Refuse | On refuse |
|---|---|---|---|
| known | 300 | 600 | no upstream call, exit 75 |
| `script:`… | 300 | 600 | no upstream call, exit 75 |
| unknown (`-`) | 300 | never | the call always runs |

Writes (merge, create, comment, edit, ready) are never refused. Each session has one small file
under `budget/` beside the call log holding at most an hour of minute buckets, so a call reads one
tiny file and never the log. `gh budget` prints the counters and the live rate limit.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import hashlib
import json
import os
import re
import subprocess
import sys
import time
from pathlib import Path

DEFAULT_TTL = 300
MAX_WAIT = 3600

# gh pr reads that cost a GraphQL request every time. Cached together below.
